IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s388-domestication`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVII:
-- section 389, "Temporary transfer of domicile into this State".
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer dg11-seat.l4 asks these rules as questions.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text). `-- src:N | ...` is line N of it.
--
-- The section lets an entity formed under foreign law (a "non-United States entity") move its DOMICILE into this State for as long as an emergency condition
-- requires, while it stays governed by its own law and managed in accordance with it. It is not a domestication (section 388): the entity does not become a Delaware corporation.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never recomputed):
--   * § 102(a)(1) (piece dg1): that the name of the entity meets the requirements of § 102(a)(1).
--   * § 321 (piece dg10): service of process on a corporation of this State.
--   * § 371 (piece dg10): what is "doing business" in this State.
--   * Chapter 100 of Title 29 (Delaware's Freedom of Information Act; not among the inputs): whether a record is open to public inspection under it.
--   * "the law of the jurisdiction the law of which governs the internal affairs" of the entity, and what it prohibits or permits: not among the inputs; BOOLEAN facts.
--   * the judgment of "the non-United States entity's management" that an emergency condition still requires the transfer (subsection (c)(4)f.): a judgment handed to the entity's management, taken as a fact.
-- Sections 388(a)(1) and (2) (this piece, dg11-s388-domestication.l4) define "foreign jurisdiction" and "non-United States entity", and subsection (a)(2) below points at them.
-- Dates are data: the dates in this section are March 1 and March 2 of each year (subsection (d)) and the 30-day periods of subsections (c) and (e).

§ `Section 389(a) - definitions`

-- src:1966 | (1) The term “emergency condition” shall be deemed to include but not be limited to any of the following:
-- src:1967 | a. War or other armed conflict;
-- src:1968 | b. Revolution or insurrection;
-- src:1969 | c. Invasion or occupation by foreign military forces;
-- src:1970 | d. Rioting or civil commotion of an extended nature;
-- src:1971 | e. Domination by a foreign power;
-- src:1972 | f. Expropriation, nationalization or confiscation of a material part of the assets or property of the non-United States entity;
-- src:1973 | g. Impairment of the institution of private property (including private property held abroad);
-- src:1974 | h. The taking of any action under the laws of the United States whereby persons resident in the jurisdiction, the law of which governs the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, might be treated as “enemies” or otherwise restricted under laws of the United States relating to trading with enemies of the United States;
-- src:1975 | i. The immediate threat of any of the foregoing; and
-- src:1976 | j. Such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile.
-- Gloss: the list is "include but not be limited to": an event on the list is an emergency condition; an event that is not on the list is NOT thereby shown not to be one, so that case is NOTHING (not covered). (Fork register F-389-3)
-- Item j. is itself conditional: the event must be one that the governing law lets the entity move its domicile on account of.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(a)(1) (src:1966-1976)
DECLARE `s 389(a)(1) Event` IS ONE OF
    `war or other armed conflict`
    `revolution or insurrection`
    `invasion or occupation by foreign military forces`
    `rioting or civil commotion of an extended nature`
    `domination by a foreign power`
    `expropriation, nationalization or confiscation of a material part of the assets or property of the non-United States entity`
    `impairment of the institution of private property, including private property held abroad`
    `the taking of any action under the laws of the United States whereby persons resident in the jurisdiction might be treated as enemies or otherwise restricted under laws of the United States relating to trading with enemies`
    `the immediate threat of any of the foregoing`
    `such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile`
    `another event that s 389(a)(1) does not list`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(a)(1) (src:1966-1976)
GIVEN event IS A `s 389(a)(1) Event`
      `the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the entity permits it to transfer its domicile on account of the event` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` event `the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the entity permits it to transfer its domicile on account of the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile` THEN
        IF `the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the entity permits it to transfer its domicile on account of the event` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `another event that s 389(a)(1) does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1977 | (2) The term “foreign jurisdiction” and the term “non-United States entity” shall have the same meanings as set forth in § 388(a) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(a)(2) (src:1977)
GIVEN place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(a)(2) the place is a foreign jurisdiction as § 388(a) defines it` place MEANS
    `s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` place

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(a)(2) (src:1977)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
      place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity as § 388(a) defines it` kind place MEANS
    `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` kind place

-- src:1978 | (3) The terms “officers” and “directors” include, in addition to such persons, trustees, managers, partners and all other persons performing functions equivalent to those of officers and directors, however named or described in any relevant instrument.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(a)(3) (src:1978)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee, a manager or a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person performs functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director, however named or described in any relevant instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` `the person is an officer or a director` `the person is a trustee, a manager or a partner` `the person performs functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director, however named or described in any relevant instrument` MEANS
        `the person is an officer or a director`
    OR  `the person is a trustee, a manager or a partner`
    OR  `the person performs functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director, however named or described in any relevant instrument`

§ `Section 389(b) - who may transfer its domicile into this State`

-- src:1979 | (b) Any non-United States entity may, subject to and upon compliance with this section, transfer its domicile (which term, as used in this section, shall be deemed to refer in addition to the seat, siege social or principal place of business or central administration of such entity, or any other equivalent thereto under applicable law) into this State, and may perform the acts described in this section, so long as the law by which the internal affairs of such entity are governed does not expressly prohibit such transfer.
-- Gloss: the entity's power; the Secretary of State's side is to accept a transfer made in compliance (an official: no seat). "Upon compliance with this section" is an input here, decided by the rules for subsections (c) to (e).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(b) (src:1979)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
      place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the entity has complied with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law by which the internal affairs of the entity are governed expressly prohibits the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` kind place `the entity has complied with this section` `the law by which the internal affairs of the entity are governed expressly prohibits the transfer` MEANS
        `s 389(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity as § 388(a) defines it` kind place
    AND `the entity has complied with this section`
    AND (NOT `the law by which the internal affairs of the entity are governed expressly prohibits the transfer`)

-- Gloss: in this section "domicile" refers in addition to the seat, the siege social, the principal place of business and the central administration, or any other equivalent under applicable law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(b) (src:1979)
DECLARE `s 389(b) Place that the entity moves` IS ONE OF
    `the domicile of the entity`
    `the seat of the entity`
    `the siege social of the entity`
    `the principal place of business of the entity`
    `the central administration of the entity`
    `another equivalent of the seat under applicable law`
    `a place of another kind that s 389(b) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(b) (src:1979)
GIVEN place IS A `s 389(b) Place that the entity moves`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a place of another kind that s 389(b) does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 389(c) - what the entity submits to the Secretary of State, and when`

-- src:1980 | (c) Any non-United States entity that shall propose to transfer its domicile into this State shall submit to the Secretary of State for the Secretary of State’s review, at least 30 days prior to the proposed transfer of domicile, the following:
-- Gloss: the submission is made at least 30 days before the proposed transfer; made exactly 30 days before is in time (Fork register F-389-1). The Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period (below).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1980)
GIVETH A Period
`s 389(c) the least time before the proposed transfer for the submission` MEANS `period in days` 30

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1980)
GIVEN `the date on which the documents were submitted to the Secretary of State` IS A DATE
      `the date of the proposed transfer of domicile` IS A DATE
      `the Secretary of State has waived the 30-day period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` `the date on which the documents were submitted to the Secretary of State` `the date of the proposed transfer of domicile` `the Secretary of State has waived the 30-day period` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State has waived the 30-day period`
    OR  (`the date on which the documents were submitted to the Secretary of State` AT MOST (`the date` `s 389(c) the least time before the proposed transfer for the submission` `before` `the date of the proposed transfer of domicile`))

-- src:1981 | (1) A copy of its certificate of incorporation and bylaws (or the equivalent thereof under applicable law), certified as true and correct by the appropriate director, officer or government official;
-- src:1982 | (2) A certificate issued by an authorized official of the jurisdiction the law of which governs the internal affairs of the non-United States entity evidencing its existence;
-- src:1983 | (3) A list indicating the person or persons who, in the event of a transfer pursuant to this section, shall be the authorized officers and directors of the non-United States entity, together with evidence of their authority to act and their respective executed agreements in writing regarding service of process as set out in subsection (j) of this section;
-- src:1984 | (4) A certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director of the non-United States entity, setting forth:
-- src:1985 | a. The name and address of its registered agent in this State;
-- src:1986 | b. A general description of the business in which it is engaged;
-- src:1987 | c. That the filing of such certificate has been duly authorized by any necessary action and does not violate the certificate of incorporation or bylaws (or equivalent thereof under applicable law) or any material agreement or instrument binding on such entity;
-- src:1988 | d. A list indicating the person or persons authorized to sign the written communications required by subsection (e) of this section;
-- src:1989 | e. An affirmance that such transfer is not expressly prohibited under the law by which the internal affairs of the non-United States entity are governed; and
-- src:1990 | f. An undertaking that any transfer of domicile into this State will take place only in the event of an emergency condition in the jurisdiction the law of which governs the internal affairs of the non-United States entity and that such transfer shall continue only so long as such emergency condition, in the judgment of the non-United States entity’s management, so requires; and
-- src:1991 | (5) The examination fee prescribed under § 391 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1981-1991)
DECLARE `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` HAS
    `the name and address of its registered agent in this State`                                                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a general description of the business in which it is engaged`                                                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `that the filing of the certificate has been duly authorized by any necessary action and does not violate its governing documents or any material agreement or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a list of the persons authorized to sign the written communications required by subsection (e)`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `an affirmance that the transfer is not expressly prohibited under the law by which its internal affairs are governed`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undertaking that any transfer will take place only in the event of an emergency condition and will continue only so long as the emergency condition, in the judgment of its management, so requires` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1981-1991)
DECLARE `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` HAS
    `copy of its certificate of incorporation and bylaws, or the equivalent, certified as true and correct by the appropriate director, officer or government official`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate issued by an authorized official of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs evidencing its existence`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `list of the persons who shall be its authorized officers and directors, with evidence of their authority and their executed agreements regarding service of process`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director`                                                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `examination fee prescribed under § 391`                                                                                                                                IS A NUMBER

-- out of range: the examination fee is § 391(a)(20) ($10,000), this piece; paying "the examination fee" is paying at least that sum.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1991); § 391(a)(20)
GIVEN submitted IS A `s 389(c) What the entity submitted`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c)(5) the examination fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid` submitted MEANS
    submitted's `examination fee prescribed under § 391` AT LEAST `s 391(a)(20) the fee on the documents prescribed in § 389(c)`

-- src:1992 | If any of the documents referred to in paragraphs (c)(1)-(5) of this section are not in English, a translation thereof, under oath of the translator, shall be attached thereto.
-- Gloss: a translation under oath of the translator is needed for any document not in English, unless the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1992)
GIVEN `any of the documents is not in English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a translation under oath of the translator is attached to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` `any of the documents is not in English` `a translation under oath of the translator is attached to it` `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement` MEANS
        (NOT `any of the documents is not in English`)
    OR  `a translation under oath of the translator is attached to it`
    OR  `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement`

-- Gloss: the documents satisfy the requirements of the section when (1) to (5) are all submitted, (4) sets forth everything a. to f., and the translation requirement is met.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1980-1992)
GIVEN submitted IS A `s 389(c) What the entity submitted`
      `sets forth` IS A `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth`
      `the translation requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` submitted `sets forth` `the translation requirement is met` MEANS
        submitted's `copy of its certificate of incorporation and bylaws, or the equivalent, certified as true and correct by the appropriate director, officer or government official`
    AND submitted's `certificate issued by an authorized official of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs evidencing its existence`
    AND submitted's `list of the persons who shall be its authorized officers and directors, with evidence of their authority and their executed agreements regarding service of process`
    AND submitted's `certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director`
    AND `s 389(c)(5) the examination fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid` submitted
    AND `sets forth`'s `the name and address of its registered agent in this State`
    AND `sets forth`'s `a general description of the business in which it is engaged`
    AND `sets forth`'s `that the filing of the certificate has been duly authorized by any necessary action and does not violate its governing documents or any material agreement or instrument`
    AND `sets forth`'s `a list of the persons authorized to sign the written communications required by subsection (e)`
    AND `sets forth`'s `an affirmance that the transfer is not expressly prohibited under the law by which its internal affairs are governed`
    AND `sets forth`'s `an undertaking that any transfer will take place only in the event of an emergency condition and will continue only so long as the emergency condition, in the judgment of its management, so requires`
    AND `the translation requirement is met`

-- src:1992 | If such documents satisfy the requirements of this section, and if the name of the non-United States entity meets the requirements of § 102(a)(1) of this title, the Secretary of State shall notify the non-United States entity that such documents have been accepted for filing, and the records of the Secretary of State shall reflect such acceptance and such notification.
-- out of range: § 102(a)(1) (piece dg1): whether the name meets its requirements is a BOOLEAN fact. The entity's side: a claim to the notification; the Secretary of State's side: the duty.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1992)
GIVEN `the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the non-United States entity meets the requirements of § 102(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the Secretary of State must notify the entity that the documents have been accepted for filing` `the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `the name of the non-United States entity meets the requirements of § 102(a)(1)` MEANS
        `the documents satisfy the requirements of this section`
    AND `the name of the non-United States entity meets the requirements of § 102(a)(1)`

-- src:1992 | In addition, the Secretary of State shall enter the name of the non-United States entity on the Secretary of State’s reserved list to remain there so long as the non-United States entity is in compliance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1992)
GIVEN `the documents have been accepted for filing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is in compliance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the name of the entity is on the Secretary of State's reserved list` `the documents have been accepted for filing` `the entity is in compliance with this section` MEANS
    `the documents have been accepted for filing` AND `the entity is in compliance with this section`

-- src:1992 | No document submitted under this subsection shall be available for public inspection pursuant to Chapter 100 of Title 29 until, and unless, such entity effects a transfer of its domicile as provided in this section.
-- Gloss: until the entity effects a transfer (and if it never does) the documents are not available under Chapter 100 of Title 29; once it has, this sentence no longer bars inspection, but it does not itself make them available
-- (that is for Chapter 100, not among the inputs), so that case is NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1992)
GIVEN `the entity has effected a transfer of its domicile as provided in this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the document submitted is available for public inspection pursuant to Chapter 100 of Title 29` `the entity has effected a transfer of its domicile as provided in this section` MEANS
    IF   `the entity has effected a transfer of its domicile as provided in this section`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1992 | The Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and translation requirement provided for in this subsection upon request by such entity, supported by facts (including, without limitation, the existence of an emergency condition) justifying such waiver.
-- Gloss: the waiver is the Secretary of State's discretion (never guessed: the actual waiver is an input above); this rule says when the Secretary of State MAY waive: on the entity's request, supported by facts that justify it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(c) (src:1992)
GIVEN `the entity has requested the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is supported by facts, including the existence of an emergency condition, justifying the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(c) the Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` `the entity has requested the waiver` `the request is supported by facts, including the existence of an emergency condition, justifying the waiver` MEANS
    `the entity has requested the waiver` AND `the request is supported by facts, including the existence of an emergency condition, justifying the waiver`

§ `Section 389(d) - the annual certificate`

-- src:1993 | (d) On or before March 1 in each year, prior to the transfer of its domicile as provided for in subsection (e) of this section, during any such transfer and, in the event that it desires to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section, after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, the non-United States entity shall file a certificate executed by an appropriate officer or director of the non-United States entity, certifying that the documents submitted pursuant to this section remain in full force and effect or attaching any amendments or supplements thereto and translated as required in subsection (c) of this section, together with the filing fee prescribed under § 391 of this title.
-- Gloss: the certificate is due in each year, at three stages: before the transfer, during it, and (only if the entity desires to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile) after its domicile has ceased to be in this State.
-- For an entity whose domicile has ceased to be in this State and which does not desire to continue, the text states no duty, so that case is NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
DECLARE `s 389(d) Stage of the entity` IS ONE OF
    `prior to the transfer of its domicile`
    `during the transfer of its domicile`
    `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it desires to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section`
    `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it does not desire to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
GIVEN stage IS A `s 389(d) Stage of the entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` stage MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    WHEN `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it does not desire to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "On or before March 1 in each year": a certificate filed on March 1 is in time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 389(d) the last day for filing the annual certificate in the year` year MEANS YearMonthDay year 3 1

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
DECLARE `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` HAS
    `certificate is executed by an appropriate officer or director of the entity`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate certifies that the documents remain in full force and effect, or attaches any amendments or supplements, translated as required in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `filing fee prescribed under § 391`                                                                                                     IS A NUMBER

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993); § 391(a)(21)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` certificate MEANS
        certificate's `certificate is executed by an appropriate officer or director of the entity`
    AND certificate's `certificate certifies that the documents remain in full force and effect, or attaches any amendments or supplements, translated as required in subsection (c)`
    AND (certificate's `filing fee prescribed under § 391` AT LEAST `s 391(a)(21) the annual fee on the documents prescribed in § 389(d)`)

-- src:1993 | In the event that any non-United States entity fails to file the required certificate on or before March 1 in each year, all certificates and filings made pursuant to this section shall become null and void on March 2 in such year, and any proposed transfer thereafter shall be subject to all of the required submissions and the examination fee set forth in subsection (c) of this section.
-- Gloss: if the certificate is not filed on or before March 1 of the year, all the entity's certificates and filings under the section are null and void from March 2 of that year; a certificate filed on March 2 or later does not save them.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the date on which the annual certificate was filed in the year, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date for which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` year `the date on which the annual certificate was filed in the year, if it has been` `the date for which the question is asked` MEANS
        (`the date for which the question is asked` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay year 3 2))
    AND (CONSIDER `the date on which the annual certificate was filed in the year, if it has been`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST filed THEN filed GREATER THAN `s 389(d) the last day for filing the annual certificate in the year` year)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(d) (src:1993)
GIVEN `the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(d) a proposed transfer is subject to all of the required submissions and the examination fee of subsection (c)` `the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` MEANS
    `the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void`

§ `Section 389(e), (f), (g), (h) - making the transfer, and its effects`

-- src:1994 | (e) If the Secretary of State accepts the documents submitted pursuant to subsection (c) of this section for filing, such entity may transfer its domicile to this State at any time by means of a written communication to such effect addressed to the Secretary of State, signed by 1 of the persons named on the list filed pursuant to paragraph (c)(4)d. of this section, and confirming that the statements made pursuant to paragraph (c)(4) of this section remain true and correct; provided, that if emergency conditions have affected ordinary means of communication, such notification may be made by telegram, telex, telecopy or other form of writing so long as a duly signed duplicate is received by the Secretary of State within 30 days thereafter.
-- Gloss: once the documents are accepted, the entity may transfer its domicile at any time by a written communication to the Secretary of State, signed by one of the persons on the (c)(4)d. list, confirming that the (c)(4) statements remain true.
-- If emergency conditions have affected ordinary means of communication, the communication may be made by telegram, telex, telecopy or another writing if a duly signed duplicate reaches the Secretary of State within 30 days thereafter (Fork register F-389-2: within 30 days after the communication).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(e) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State accepted the documents for filing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is in writing, addressed to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by 1 of the persons named on the list filed pursuant to paragraph (c)(4)d.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it confirms that the statements made pursuant to paragraph (c)(4) remain true and correct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by the ordinary means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `emergency conditions have affected the ordinary means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the communication` IS A DATE
      `the date on which a duly signed duplicate was received by the Secretary of State, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` `the Secretary of State accepted the documents for filing` `the communication is in writing, addressed to the Secretary of State` `it is signed by 1 of the persons named on the list filed pursuant to paragraph (c)(4)d.` `it confirms that the statements made pursuant to paragraph (c)(4) remain true and correct` `it was made by the ordinary means of communication` `emergency conditions have affected the ordinary means of communication` `the date of the communication` `the date on which a duly signed duplicate was received by the Secretary of State, if it was` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State accepted the documents for filing`
    AND `the communication is in writing, addressed to the Secretary of State`
    AND `it is signed by 1 of the persons named on the list filed pursuant to paragraph (c)(4)d.`
    AND `it confirms that the statements made pursuant to paragraph (c)(4) remain true and correct`
    AND (    `it was made by the ordinary means of communication`
          OR (    `emergency conditions have affected the ordinary means of communication`
              AND (CONSIDER `the date on which a duly signed duplicate was received by the Secretary of State, if it was`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                   WHEN JUST received THEN received AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date of the communication`))))

-- src:1994 | The records of the Secretary of State shall reflect the fact of such transfer.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(e) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(e) the records of the Secretary of State must reflect the transfer` `the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` MEANS
    `the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State`

-- src:1994 | Upon the payment to the Secretary of State of the fee prescribed under § 391 of this title, the Secretary of State shall certify that the non-United States entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title.
-- Gloss: the fee here is the one § 391 prescribes (this piece: the annual fee of § 391(a)(21) and the examination fee of § 391(a)(20) are the two it fixes for this section); the payment is a fact.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(e) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(e) the Secretary of State must certify that the entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` `the fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid to the Secretary of State` MEANS
    `the fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid to the Secretary of State`

-- src:1994 | Such certificate of the Secretary of State shall be prima facie evidence of transfer by such non-United States entity of its domicile into this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(e) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(e) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer of the domicile into this State` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate`

-- src:1995 | (f) Except to the extent expressly prohibited by the laws of this State, from and after the time that a non-United States entity transfers its domicile to this State pursuant to this section, the non-United States entity shall have all of the powers which it had immediately prior to such transfer under the law of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs and the directors and officers designated pursuant to paragraph (c)(3) of this section, and their successors, may manage the business and affairs of the non-United States entity in accordance with the laws of such jurisdiction.
-- Gloss: after the transfer the entity has all the powers it had before under the law governing its internal affairs, except to the extent the laws of this State expressly prohibit; and the directors and officers designated under (c)(3), and their successors, may manage its business and affairs under that law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(f) (src:1995)
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of this State expressly prohibit the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(f) the entity has the power that it had immediately prior to the transfer` `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section` `the laws of this State expressly prohibit the power` MEANS
    IF   `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the laws of this State expressly prohibit the power`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(f) (src:1995)
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer designated pursuant to paragraph (c)(3), or a successor of one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(f) the person may manage the business and affairs of the entity in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs` `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section` `the person is a director or officer designated pursuant to paragraph (c)(3), or a successor of one` MEANS
    IF   `the entity has transferred its domicile to this State pursuant to this section` AND `the person is a director or officer designated pursuant to paragraph (c)(3), or a successor of one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1995 | Any such activity conducted pursuant to this section shall not be deemed to be doing business within this State for purposes of § 371 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(f) (src:1995)
GIVEN `the activity is conducted pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(f) the activity is deemed to be doing business within this State for purposes of § 371` `the activity is conducted pursuant to this section` MEANS
    IF   `the activity is conducted pursuant to this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1995 | Any reference in this section to the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of a non-United States entity which has transferred its domicile into this State shall be deemed to be a reference to such law as in effect immediately prior to the transfer of domicile.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(f) (src:1995)
DECLARE `s 389(f) Version of the law governing the internal affairs` IS ONE OF
    `the law as in effect immediately prior to the transfer of domicile`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(f) (src:1995)
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 389(f) Version of the law governing the internal affairs`
`s 389(f) the version of the law to which a reference in this section is a reference` `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` MEANS
    IF   `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State`
    THEN JUST `the law as in effect immediately prior to the transfer of domicile`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1996 | (g) For purposes of any action in the courts of this State, no non-United States entity which has obtained the certificate of the Secretary of State referred to in subsection (e) of this section shall be deemed to be an “enemy” person or entity for any purpose, including, without limitation, in relation to any claim of title to its assets, wherever located, or to its ability to institute suit in said courts.
-- Gloss: in an action in the courts of this State, an entity holding the Secretary of State's certificate is not an "enemy" for any purpose, including a claim of title to its assets and its ability to sue. Without the certificate: not addressed, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(g) (src:1996)
GIVEN `the question arises in an action in the courts of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity has obtained the certificate of the Secretary of State referred to in subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(g) the entity is deemed to be an enemy person or entity` `the question arises in an action in the courts of this State` `the entity has obtained the certificate of the Secretary of State referred to in subsection (e)` MEANS
    IF   `the question arises in an action in the courts of this State` AND `the entity has obtained the certificate of the Secretary of State referred to in subsection (e)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1997 | (h) The transfer by any non-United States entity of its domicile into this State shall not be deemed to affect any obligations or liabilities of such non-United States entity incurred prior to such transfer.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(h) (src:1997)
GIVEN `the obligation or liability was incurred prior to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(h) the transfer leaves the obligation or liability unaffected` `the obligation or liability was incurred prior to the transfer` MEANS
    IF   `the obligation or liability was incurred prior to the transfer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 389(i), (j), (k) - distributions, service of process, withdrawal`

-- src:1998 | (i) The directors of any non-United States entity which has transferred its domicile into this State may withhold from any holder of equity interests in such entity any amounts payable to such holder on account of dividends or other distributions, if the directors shall determine that such holder will not have the full benefit of such payment, so long as the directors shall make provision for the retention of such withheld payment in escrow or under some similar arrangement for the benefit of such holder.
-- Gloss: the directors' power, and the holder's liability to it: they may withhold a dividend or other distribution payable to the holder if they determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of it, so long as they provide for its retention in escrow
-- or under a similar arrangement for the holder's benefit. The determination is the directors' (a fact the caller states), never guessed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(i) (src:1998)
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is payable to the holder of equity interests on account of dividends or other distributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors make provision for the retention of the withheld payment in escrow or under some similar arrangement for the benefit of the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` `the amount is payable to the holder of equity interests on account of dividends or other distributions` `the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment` `the directors make provision for the retention of the withheld payment in escrow or under some similar arrangement for the benefit of the holder` MEANS
        `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State`
    AND `the amount is payable to the holder of equity interests on account of dividends or other distributions`
    AND `the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment`
    AND `the directors make provision for the retention of the withheld payment in escrow or under some similar arrangement for the benefit of the holder`

-- src:1999 | (j) All process issued out of any court of this State, all orders made by any court of this State and all rules and notices of any kind required to be served on any non-United States entity which has transferred its domicile into this State may be served on the non-United States entity pursuant to § 321 of this title in the same manner as if such entity were a corporation of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(j) (src:1999)
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389(j) process, orders, rules and notices may be served on the entity pursuant to § 321 as if it were a corporation of this State` `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State` MEANS
    IF   `the entity has transferred its domicile into this State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1999 | The directors of a non-United States entity which has transferred its domicile into this State shall agree in writing that they will be amenable to service of process by the same means as, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State to the same extent as are directors of corporations of this State, and such agreements shall be submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before the respective directors take office.
-- Gloss: each director agrees IN WRITING to be amenable to service of process, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State, as a director of a corporation of this State is; and the agreement is submitted to the Secretary of State for filing BEFORE the director takes office.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(j) (src:1999)
GIVEN `the director has agreed in writing to be amenable to service of process by the same means as, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State to the same extent as, directors of corporations of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement was submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before the director took office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(j) the director has done what the section requires before taking office` `the director has agreed in writing to be amenable to service of process by the same means as, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State to the same extent as, directors of corporations of this State` `the agreement was submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before the director took office` MEANS
        `the director has agreed in writing to be amenable to service of process by the same means as, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State to the same extent as, directors of corporations of this State`
    AND `the agreement was submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before the director took office`

-- src:2000 | (k) Any non-United States entity which has transferred its domicile into this State may voluntarily return to the jurisdiction the law of which governs its internal affairs by filing with the Secretary of State an application to withdraw from this State.
-- src:2000 | Such application shall be accompanied by a resolution of the directors of the non-United States entity authorizing such withdrawal and by a certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of such jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating the consent of such jurisdiction to such withdrawal.
-- src:2000 | The application shall also contain, or be accompanied by, the agreement of the non-United States entity that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the non-United States entity arising prior to its withdrawal from this State, which agreement shall include the appointment of the Secretary of State as the agent of the non-United States entity to accept service of process in any such proceeding and shall specify the address to which a copy of process served upon the Secretary of State shall be mailed.
-- Gloss: the application to withdraw is accompanied by (1) a resolution of the directors authorizing the withdrawal, (2) a certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of the jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating that jurisdiction's consent, and
-- (3) the entity's agreement that it may be served with process in this State on obligations arising before withdrawal, appointing the Secretary of State as its agent and specifying the address for a copy of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(k) (src:2000)
DECLARE `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` HAS
    `resolution of the directors authorizing the withdrawal`                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of the jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating its consent`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreement that the entity may be served with process in this State on obligations arising prior to withdrawal`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment of the Secretary of State as the agent of the entity to accept service of process in such a proceeding`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the address to which a copy of process served upon the Secretary of State shall be mailed`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(k) (src:2000)
GIVEN application IS A `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` application MEANS
        application's `resolution of the directors authorizing the withdrawal`
    AND application's `certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of the jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating its consent`
    AND application's `agreement that the entity may be served with process in this State on obligations arising prior to withdrawal`
    AND application's `appointment of the Secretary of State as the agent of the entity to accept service of process in such a proceeding`
    AND application's `the address to which a copy of process served upon the Secretary of State shall be mailed`

-- src:2000 | Upon the payment of any fees and taxes owed to this State, the Secretary of State shall file the application and the non-United States entity’s domicile shall, as of the time of filing, cease to be in this State.
-- Gloss: on payment of any fees and taxes owed to this State the Secretary of State files the application, and the entity's domicile ceases to be in this State as of the time of filing.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(k) (src:2000)
GIVEN `the application to withdraw is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any fees and taxes owed to this State have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(k) the Secretary of State must file the application to withdraw` `the application to withdraw is complete` `any fees and taxes owed to this State have been paid` MEANS
    `the application to withdraw is complete` AND `any fees and taxes owed to this State have been paid`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 389(k) (src:2000)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has filed the application to withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time in question is at or after the time of filing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 389(k) the domicile of the entity has ceased to be in this State` `the Secretary of State has filed the application to withdraw` `the time in question is at or after the time of filing` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has filed the application to withdraw` AND `the time in question is at or after the time of filing`
